  "id": "Compound::DB01189 - Gene::2560",
  "verbalization": "Desflurane, an organofluorine anesthetic agent, is linked to Gabrb1 through a shared pathway involving Isoflurane. The evidence suggests that Desflurane is involved in the pathophysiology of Breath Holding Attack or Breath Holding, which are mediated by Isoflurane. Isoflurane, in turn, binds to Gabrb1, indicating a potential mechanism by which Desflurane may influence Gabrb1 activity. The lowest common ancestors of Desflurane and Isoflurane are both classified as Organofluorine Compounds and Anesthetic Agents, suggesting a common pharmacological profile. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Desflurane in modulating Gabrb1 signaling through its interaction with Isoflurane, potentially affecting neuronal function or other physiological processes. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between Desflurane and Gabrb1, mediated through Isoflurane, and underscores the importance of anesthetic agents in influencing receptor activity.",
